	<!--
	  Quick Capture (screenshot + highlight OCR) is a Developer ID / DMG-only
	  feature. It is gated OFF in the Mac App Store build via
	  DistributionMode.isAppStore, so the MAS build never exercises the
	  screen-capture code path and never requests the permission at runtime.

	  NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription supplies the purpose string macOS shows
	  when the DMG build first captures the screen for OCR-based capture. It is
	  harmless in the MAS build (no capture APIs are invoked there).

	  There is intentionally NO Accessibility Info.plist key: macOS gates
	  Accessibility (for the global hotkey / synthetic events used by highlight
	  capture) through the standard AXIsProcessTrusted TCC prompt, not an
	  Info.plist usage string. That permission is requested only at runtime in
	  the DMG build and never in the MAS build.
	-->
	<key>NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Cortex captures a region of your screen to read highlighted text so you can save it to your memory. This feature is optional and only runs when you trigger a capture.</string>
</dict>
